{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "topo-header",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1670,
      "y": -2200,
      "width": 3340,
      "height": 250,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n# Topological foundations: from definitions to usable theorems\n\nRead four routes: basic language, local set structure, sequences and continuity, then compactness and connectedness. Concept cards link to definitions; separate cards explain criteria and limits. First fix the setting: a topological space, a metric space, or finite-dimensional Euclidean space.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n# 拓扑基础：从定义到可用定理\n\n从上到下读四条主线：基础语言 → 集合局部结构 → 序列与连续 → 紧致、连通及其应用。每个通用概念节点都直达定义；等价判别、边界和应用定理各自独立。\n\n**先确认环境：一般拓扑、度量空间，还是有限维欧氏空间。**",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-metric",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -4395,
      "y": 1915,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 280,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[度量空间|Metric space]]\n\nA finite, nonnegative distance separates points, is symmetric and obeys the triangle inequality. Open balls impose a strict distance threshold.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n距离有限、非负，区分不同点，对称且满足三角不等式。开球收集距离严格小于半径的点。",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-open",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -3395,
      "y": 415,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 310,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[开集|Open set]]\n\nIn a metric space, each member has a ball staying inside the set; radii may vary by point. In a general topology, open sets belong to the specified family.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n度量空间中每个成员都有留在集合内的球，半径可随点变化；一般拓扑中，开集是指定开集族的成员。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-topology",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -195,
      "y": -85,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 280,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[拓扑|Topology]]\n\nA family of subsets containing the empty and whole space, closed under arbitrary unions and finite intersections. A metric is one way to generate it.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n包含空集与全空间、对任意并和有限交封闭的子集族；度量是生成拓扑的一种方式。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-closed",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2205,
      "y": 615,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[闭集|Closed set]]\n\n$F$ is closed in $X$ when $X\\setminus F$ is open in $X$. A set can be both open and closed, or neither.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n闭性由同一环境空间中的开补集定义。集合可以既开又闭，也可以既不开也不闭。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-closed-ops",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2205,
      "y": -685,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[闭集运算|Operations on closed sets]]\n\nWithin one fixed space, arbitrary intersections and finite unions of closed sets are closed. An infinite union need not be closed.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n同一环境中，闭集的任意交和有限并仍闭；无限并不保证闭。",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-subspace",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1695,
      "y": 415,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 280,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[子空间拓扑|Subspace topology]]\n\nFor $Y\\subseteq X$, its open sets are $Y\\cap U$ with $U$ open in $X$. In a metric subspace, balls are also restricted by intersecting with $Y$.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n子空间的开集由环境开集与子空间取交得到；度量子空间的球也要取交，开闭判断随环境改变。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-interior",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -195,
      "y": -1085,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[集合内部|Interior of a set]]\n\nThe largest open subset contained in the set. A point is interior if some open neighbourhood around it stays inside the set.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n集合所含的最大开集。内点周围存在一个完全留在集合内的开邻域；须指明环境。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-closure",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3405,
      "y": 115,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[集合闭包|Closure of a set]]\n\nThe smallest closed superset. Every open neighbourhood of a closure point meets the set, possibly at that point itself.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n包含原集合的最小闭集。闭包点的每个开邻域都碰到集合，可以只碰到该点自身。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-boundary",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3405,
      "y": -1085,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 260,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[集合边界|Boundary of a set]]\n\nEvery open neighbourhood meets both the set and its complement. Equivalently, take the closure and remove the interior in the same space.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n每个开邻域都碰到集合及其补集；等价于在同一环境中用闭包减去内部。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-closure-seq",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 4405,
      "y": 4115,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 340,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[闭包的序列判别|Sequential test for closure]]\n\nFor $A\\subseteq X$ in a metric space, $x\\in X$ lies in the closure of $A$ exactly when some sequence in $A$ converges to $x$. Repeated terms are allowed.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n度量空间中，$x$ 属于 $A$ 的闭包，当且仅当存在各项都在 $A$ 中且收敛到 $x$ 的序列；允许重复取值。",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-closed-seq",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 3005,
      "y": 2915,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 350,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[闭集的序列判别|Sequential test for closed sets]]\n\nIn a metric space $X$, a subset $F$ is closed exactly when every sequence in $F$ that converges in $X$ has its limit in $F$. Not every sequence must converge.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n度量空间 $X$ 中，$F$ 闭，当且仅当每条来自 $F$ 且在 $X$ 中收敛的序列，其极限仍在 $F$ 内；不要求每条序列都收敛。",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-equivalent-metrics",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -5395,
      "y": 1910,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[拓扑等价度量|Topologically equivalent metrics]]\n\nTwo metrics on the same set give exactly the same open sets. They preserve sequence limits and continuous maps, but need not preserve numerical distances or boundedness.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n同一集合上的两个度量产生完全相同的开集，因而保持序列极限与连续映射，却未必保持数值距离或有界性。",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-sequence",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -195,
      "y": 4910,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 330,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[序列收敛|Sequence convergence]]\n\nFor every tolerance $\\varepsilon>0$, one cutoff makes every later term less than $\\varepsilon$ from the limit. The limit must belong to the specified metric space.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n每个容许误差 $\\varepsilon>0$ 都对应一个门槛，之后所有项距极限都小于 $\\varepsilon$。极限必须属于所指定的度量空间。",
      "color": "2"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-limit-unique",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1195,
      "y": 5710,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[序列极限唯一|Uniqueness of sequence limits]]\n\nIn a metric space, a convergent sequence has at most one limit. The triangle inequality separates distinct candidates. This theorem does not guarantee that a sequence converges.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n度量空间中，收敛序列至多有一个极限；三角不等式排除两个不同候选。定理不保证序列一定收敛。",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-cluster-not-limit",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 805,
      "y": 5710,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 350,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[聚点不等于收敛|Cluster points versus convergence]]\n\nIn a metric space, every ball about a sequence cluster point contains arbitrarily late terms. Convergence requires the entire tail in each ball; a convergent subsequence does not ensure this.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n度量空间中，序列聚点的每个球都含索引任意大的项；整列收敛却要求每个球都含整个充分靠后的尾部。有收敛子列并不足够。",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-continuity",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -995,
      "y": 1310,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 350,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[连续性|Continuity]]\n\nA map $f:X\\to Y$ between topological spaces is continuous when preimages of open sets in the codomain $Y$ are open in the domain $X$. Forward images need not be open.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n拓扑空间之间的映射 $f:X\\to Y$ 连续，是指陪域 $Y$ 中开集的原像在定义域 $X$ 中开；正向像不必开。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-continuity-tests",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1195,
      "y": 2910,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 360,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[连续性的等价判别|Equivalent continuity tests]]\n\nBetween metric spaces, $\\varepsilon$–$\\delta$ control, open-set preimages, closed-set preimages and preservation of all sequence limits are equivalent. The sequential converse is not guaranteed in arbitrary topology.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n度量空间之间，$\\varepsilon$–$\\delta$、开集原像、闭集原像及保持所有序列极限四种判据等价。一般拓扑中不能无条件反用序列判据。",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-compact",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 605,
      "y": 1310,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 310,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[紧致性|Compactness]]\n\nA space is compact when every open cover contains a finite subcover. The quantifier ranges over all open covers, not just one convenient cover.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n每个开覆盖都含有限子覆盖才叫紧致；必须检验所有开覆盖，不能只找一个方便的覆盖。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-seq-compact",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1005,
      "y": 3110,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 350,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[紧致性的序列判别|Sequential compactness]]\n\nIn metric spaces, compactness is equivalent to every sequence having a convergent subsequence whose limit stays in the set. This equivalence does not hold in arbitrary topology.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n度量空间中，紧致等价于每条序列都有极限仍在集合内的收敛子列；任意拓扑中不能直接使用此等价。",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-heine",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1605,
      "y": 1610,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 350,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[Heine–Borel 定理的边界|Heine–Borel theorem]]\n\nFor $K\\subseteq\\mathbb R^n$ with the usual Euclidean metric and finite $n\\ge1$, compactness is equivalent to closedness and boundedness. General metric spaces retain only the forward implication.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n有限维欧氏空间中，紧致等价于闭且有界；一般度量空间只保证紧致推出闭且有界。",
      "color": "1"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-compact-image",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -195,
      "y": 2110,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[连续像保持紧致|Compact continuous images]]\n\nA continuous map sends a compact domain to a compact image with the codomain's subspace topology. The codomain itself need not be compact.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n连续映射的紧致定义域具有紧致像，像取陪域的子空间拓扑；不保证整个陪域紧致。",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-extreme",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -195,
      "y": 3010,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[极值定理|Extreme value theorem]]\n\nA continuous real-valued function on a nonempty compact domain attains both global extreme values. Maximizing or minimizing points need not be unique.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n非空紧致定义域上的连续实值函数取得全局最大值和最小值；取得极值的点未必唯一。",
      "color": "3"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-connected",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1895,
      "y": 1110,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 310,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[连通性|Connectedness]]\n\nA space is connected when no two disjoint, nonempty sets open in that space cover it. For a subset, use its relative topology.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n不能由两个不交、非空的开集覆盖全空间，才叫连通；对子集使用相对拓扑。",
      "color": "4"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-connected-image",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1695,
      "y": 2110,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 320,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[连续像保持连通|Connected continuous images]]\n\nA continuous map sends a connected domain to a connected image. This concerns attained outputs; unused parts of the codomain need not be connected.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n连续映射把连通定义域映成连通像；结论针对实际输出，不保证整个陪域连通。",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-real-interval",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2695,
      "y": 1310,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 350,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[实线连通集是区间|Connected subsets of the real line]]\n\nIn the usual real line, a nonempty subset is connected exactly when it contains every point between any two members. Singleton sets count as intervals here.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n通常实线中，非空子集连通当且仅当包含任意两点之间的全部点；这里把单点也计作区间。",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-ivt",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -2595,
      "y": 2500,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 310,
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[介值定理|Intermediate values]]\n\nA continuous real-valued map on a connected domain attains every value between two attained outputs. This [[介值定理只保证存在性|existence conclusion]] alone supplies neither uniqueness nor an algorithm.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n连通定义域上的连续实值映射，不会跳过两个已取输出之间的值。[[介值定理只保证存在性|存在性不自动给出唯一性或算法]]。",
      "color": "6"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-total-bounded",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 605,
      "y": 2210,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 350,
      "color": "4",
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[全有界性|Total boundedness]]\n\nFor each $\\varepsilon>0$, finitely many radius-$\\varepsilon$ balls centred in the set cover it. Compact metric sets satisfy this; bounded sets need not.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n对每个正半径，都能用有限多个以集内点为中心的球覆盖集合；度量紧集满足它，有界集未必满足。"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-supremum",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2205,
      "y": 2210,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 320,
      "color": "2",
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[上确界|Supremum]]\n\nThe least upper bound bounds every member and is no larger than any other upper bound. It need not belong to the set; a maximum must.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n最小上界既界住全部成员，又不高于任何其他上界。它未必属于集合，而最大值必须属于集合。"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-real-completeness",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2805,
      "y": 2210,
      "width": 390,
      "height": 330,
      "color": "5",
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[实数的确界性质|Real least-upper-bound property]]\n\nEvery nonempty set of real numbers bounded above has a real supremum. This is an existence guarantee; it does not guarantee a maximum.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n非空且有上界的实数集合必有实数上确界。这保证存在最小上界，不保证最大值存在。"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-uniform-continuity",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1195,
      "y": 3710,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 360,
      "color": "4",
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[一致连续|Uniform continuity]]\n\nBetween metric spaces, each output tolerance $\\varepsilon>0$ admits one input tolerance $\\delta>0$ that works for every input pair. The threshold may depend on $\\varepsilon$, but not on the pair.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n度量空间之间，对每个输出容限 $\\varepsilon>0$，存在适用于所有输入对的共同输入门槛 $\\delta>0$。门槛可依赖 $\\varepsilon$，不能依赖具体输入对。"
    },
    {
      "id": "topo-compact-uniform",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -195,
      "y": 3710,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 360,
      "color": "5",
      "text": "<!-- bilingual-en:start -->\n## [[连续函数在紧致集上一致连续|Uniformity from compactness]]\n\nA continuous map from a compact metric domain into any metric space is uniformly continuous. Finite closed real intervals are compact; the output space need not be compact.\n<!-- bilingual-en:end -->\n\n紧致度量定义域上的连续映射，若陪域为任意度量空间，就一致连续。有限闭实区间是紧致定义域；不要求整个输出空间紧致。"
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
    {
      "id": "topo-edge-metric-open",
      "fromNode": "topo-metric",
      "fromSide": "top",
      "toNode": "topo-open",
      "toSide": "bottom",
      "label": "Pointwise balls define metric openness · 逐点开球定义度量开性"
    },
